  "blocks": {
    "\"The agent can't see the staging DB schema.\"": "“智能体看不到预发布数据库的 schema。”",
    "\"Wire it into the environment — give it a psql tool scoped to read-only on staging. The harness is fine, it just has nothing to act on.\"": "“把数据库接入环境：提供一个仅能只读访问预发布环境的 <code>psql</code> 工具。运行框架本身没有问题，只是目前没有可供它操作的对象。”",
    "Avoid: using \"environment\" for the runtime or the harness itself — the harness is the wrapper, the environment is the workspace.": "<em>避免：</em>用“环境”指代运行时或运行框架本身。运行框架是外层包装，环境才是工作空间。",
    "The agent only sees the environment when it looks. Everything it knows about the environment arrived through a tool result, so its picture is a collection of snapshots, each accurate at the moment it was taken. If a file changes after the agent read it — you edit it by hand, a build step regenerates it — the agent keeps reasoning from the stale copy until something prompts a re-read. An agent confidently describing a file that no longer looks like that is usually this: the environment moved, the snapshot didn't.": "智能体只有在主动查看时才能看到环境。它对环境的全部认知都来自工具结果，因此脑中的图景其实是一组快照，每张快照只在获取的那个时刻准确。如果文件在智能体读取后发生变化——例如你手动编辑，或构建步骤重新生成——智能体仍会依据旧副本推理，直到某个操作促使它重新读取。智能体信心十足地描述一个早已变样的文件，通常就是因为环境已经变化，而快照没有更新。",
    "The environment is also the layer that persists — the only one that is always stateful. A session's context is gone when the session ends, but files written to the environment remain for the next session to read — which is what memory systems, handoff artifacts, and AGENTS.md rely on. Anything an agent should still know tomorrow has to end up in the environment.": "环境也是负责持久化的层级——唯一始终<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/stateful\">有状态</a>的一层。<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/session\">会话</a>结束后，其中的上下文会消失；写入环境的文件却会保留下来，供下次会话读取。<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/memory-system\">记忆系统</a>、<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/handoff-artifact\">交接产物</a>和 AGENTS.md 都依赖这一点。凡是智能体明天仍需知道的内容，最终都必须进入环境。",
    "The world the agent acts on — anything outside the harness that the agent perceives through tool results and changes through tool calls. The harness runs the agent; the environment is what the agent works in. A file like AGENTS.md lives in the environment; the harness is what loads it into the context window. A filesystem is the most common kind of environment, but not the only one (a database, a remote API, a browser session can all be environments).": "环境是<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/agent\">智能体</a>实际操作的世界：位于<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/harness\">运行框架</a>之外、智能体通过<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/tool-result\">工具结果</a>感知并通过<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/tool-call\">工具调用</a>改变的一切。运行框架负责运行智能体，环境则是智能体开展工作的地方。<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/agents-md\">AGENTS.md</a> 之类的文件存在于环境中，运行框架负责把它加载进<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/context-window\">上下文窗口</a>。<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/filesystem\">文件系统</a>是最常见的环境，但并非唯一形式；数据库、远程 API 和浏览器会话都可以成为环境。",
    "Usage:": "<em>用法：</em>",
    "You decide how big the environment is. A sandbox shrinks it, limiting what the agent can reach; adding a tool extends it, bringing a database or an API into reach. What's inside the boundary is what the agent can perceive and change; everything outside it doesn't exist for the agent. How well the environment is set up to support the agent's work is the codebase's AX.": "环境的范围由你决定。<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/sandbox\">沙箱</a>会缩小环境，限制智能体能够触达的内容；添加<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/tool\">工具</a>则会扩展环境，把数据库或 API 纳入可操作范围。边界以内是智能体能够感知和改变的世界，边界以外对它而言并不存在。环境对智能体工作的支持程度，就是代码库的 <a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/ax\">AX</a>。"
  },
